# The variables this app reads at runtime on the VPS. Names only; never put values here.
# Each one needs two things:
#   - a repo secret (or, if it isn't secret, a repo variable) named ENV_<NAME>, and
#   - a matching line in the "Write .env" step of .github/workflows/build-and-deploy.yml.
# ENV_PAYLOAD_SECRET below becomes PAYLOAD_SECRET in the .env the deploy writes on the VPS.
# For local development use the .env.example in the repo root instead.

# Required. Signs Payload's login tokens (secret). Changing it signs everyone out.
PAYLOAD_SECRET=
# Required. Password of the database's payload user (secret). Letters and digits only: it goes into a
# connection URL. Postgres only reads it when the db-data volume is first created, so changing it
# later locks the app out of its database.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
